    <Option type="Map">
      <Option type="QString" value="198,126,72,255" name="color"/>
      <Option type="QString" value="BEST PRACTICE FOR THE APPLICATION OF AS4QGIS&#xa;_________________________________________________&#xa;&#xa;A. Data Recording In-Field and Post-Processing In-Office&#xa;A.1 Use Only ArchSurv-Code (10-digit string)&#xa;Do not reuse identical &quot;shpcontain&quot; / Shape-Containers (= first 7 digits of ArchSurv-String) for different features.&#xa;&#xa;Understand the structure of the ArchSurv-String, which consists of four parts:&#xa;'XXXX' / 'Y' / 'ZZ' / '001'&#xa;&#xa;Example: &quot;0001A03001&quot;&#xa;1st partition 'XXXX' (4 digits): Feature ID (e.g. '0001')&#xa;2nd partition 'Y' (1 letter): Container for a single line measurement / Point-Property of a Point. (e.g. 'A')&#xa;3rd partition 'ZZ' (2 digits): Measurement type code (e.g. '03')&#xa;4th partition '001' (3 digits): Continuous measurement number, starting at 001 for each new line. (e.g. '001')&#xa;&#xa;A.2 Geometries defined by the 3rd Partition (Shape-Type / &quot;shptype&quot;)&#xa;A.2.1 Point Measurements&#xa;Code; Example; Description&#xa;01 / 0023A01003 / Heights (point defines elevation for a layer)&#xa;51 / 0333C51070 / Samples (letter indicates sample method, e.g. 'C' = C14 sample)&#xa;06 or 61 / 0234D61027 / Postholes (letter defines diameter; D=4 cm)&#xa;71 / 0040C71089 / Finds (Find No.89)&#xa;81 / 0127X81006 / Photogrammetry markers (Marker No.6)&#xa;91 / 9999B91027 / Fixed points (use layer 9999 for fixed points &amp; excavation extents)&#xa;00 / 0058Y00001 / Section nails (measure two nails for automatic section polyline)&#xa;&#xa;A.2.2 Polylines&#xa;Code / Example / Description&#xa;02 / 0023A02034 / Open line&#xa;33 / 0123C33001 / Closed line in polylines-output&#xa;52 / 0023A52003 / Open line for samples (record samples with code 51 as points)&#xa;72 / 0027A72006 / Open line for finds (record finds with code 71 as points)&#xa;92 / 9999C92012 / Open line for trench extents&#xa;&#xa;A.2.3 Polygons&#xa;Code / Example / Description&#xa;03 / 0452A03027 / Closed line&#xa;53 / 0023A53003 / Closed line for samples&#xa;73 / 0027A73006 / Closed line for finds&#xa;93 / 9999A93037 / Closed line for trench extents&#xa;&#xa;B.  How to Use AS4 QGIS&#xa;B.1 Load Your Data&#xa;Load Your Data as a .csv or any other format. As long as there is an attribute column containing the &quot;ArchSurv-String&quot; and (optionally) &quot;Code&quot;-String, the algorithm will work.&#xa;&#xa;Totalstation setup --> If the recording of the total station setup is desired, the setup can be defined by a name that contains either a period &quot;.&quot;, a hyphen &quot;-&quot;, or an underscore &quot;_&quot;.  For example: '20251019_1' or '20300417.1'.&#xa;&#xa;B.2 Run AS4QGIS Algorithm&#xa;B.2.1 Choose a directory or generate virtual layers for output shapefiles.&#xa;&#xa;B.2.3 Execute AS4QGIS:&#xa;Parameters:&#xa;There are two Drop-Downs -->&#xa;- &quot;ArchSurv-String&quot;: Choose the attribute column containing the AchSurv-String.&#xa;- &quot;Code&quot;: Advised, but optionally, choose the attribute column containing the Code.&#xa;There is one Checkbox -->&#xa;- &quot;Mirror polygon geometries to polylines&quot;: If you check this box, polygons will be mirrored into the output-file &quot;polylines&quot;.&#xa;&#xa;Execution:&#xa;Review the log for any red warnings indicating filtered-out data. If important data was filtered, correct the source file to comply with &quot;ArchSurv-String&quot; structure.&#xa;&#xa;B.3 Post-Processing&#xa;Your data will appear within 4 output-files: &quot;vertices&quot; / &quot;pointdata&quot; / &quot;polylines&quot; / &quot;polygons&quot;.&#xa;Copy and paste outputs into your main project GeoPackage (.gpkg) or Shapefile (.shp).&#xa;" name="component_description"/>
