      <Option type="QString" value="226,178,74,255" name="color"/>
      <Option type="QString" value="Finds &quot;ShpType&quot; = '71'&#xa;________________________&#xa;The '71' shptype refers to finds. Similar to the posthole shptype, the letter preceding '71' defines the material, function, or category of the find.&#xa;Alongside common predefined finds materials, letters 'P' through 'W' are reserved for excavation-specific find categories. Letter 'Y' is reserved for (soil-/mortar-)samples. If no in-field find categorization is desired, the letter 'A' should be used, which represents &quot;undeclared&quot;.&#xa;&#xa;Code | Description&#xa;A71 | undeclared&#xa;B71 | metal&#xa;C71 | coin&#xa;D71 | stone object&#xa;E71 | silex&#xa;F71 | iron&#xa;G71 | glass&#xa;H71 | homo&#xa;I71 | animal bones&#xa;J71 | architectural ceramics&#xa;K71 | ceramics&#xa;L71 | burnt daub&#xa;M71 | mortar&#xa;N71 | slag&#xa;O71 | organic&#xa;P71 | excavation-specific category 1&#xa;Q71 | excavation-specific category 2&#xa;R71 | excavation-specific category 3&#xa;S71 | excavation-specific category 4&#xa;T71 | excavation-specific category 5&#xa;U71 | excavation-specific category 6&#xa;V71 | excavation-specific category 7&#xa;W71 | excavation-specific category 8&#xa;X71 | excavation-specific category 9&#xa;Y71 | sample&#xa;Z71 | miscellaneous&#xa;&#xa;_______________&#xa;Notes on shptypes '72' and '73':&#xa;Codes '72' and '73' generate find-specific polylines but do not generate polygons. When these codes are used, it is recommended to also record a corresponding point measurement with code '71' for detailed find information.&#xa;" name="component_description"/>
