    <Option type="Map">
      <Option type="QString" value="226,178,74,255" name="color"/>
      <Option type="QString" value="Sample Code '51' in ArchSurv&#xa;__________________________&#xa;The '51' geometry type allows the in-field definition of the sample method, material, or any excavation-specific category via the letter character prefix. Alongside predefined common sample methods labeled 'A' to 'J', letters from 'K' to 'Z' are reserved for excavation-specific sample categories.&#xa;If no specific in-field sample categorization is desired, the letter 'A' should be used, which is defined as &quot;undeclared sample&quot;.&#xa;&#xa;Code | Description&#xa;A51 | undeclared sample&#xa;B51 | brick sample&#xa;C51 | C14 sample&#xa;D51 | dendro sample&#xa;E51 | soil bulk sample&#xa;F51 | soil block sample&#xa;G51 | soil core sample&#xa;H51 | soil monolith sample&#xa;I51 | soil Kubiena sample&#xa;J51 | soil waterlogged sample&#xa;K51 | excavation-specific method 1&#xa;L51 | excavation-specific method 2&#xa;...&#x9;...&#xa;Codes '52' and '53' are used to generate find-specific polylines but do not generate polygons. If these codes are used, it is recommended to also record a corresponding point measurement using the '51' code for sample data." name="component_description"/>
