    <Option type="Map">
      <Option type="QString" value="236,201,119,255" name="color"/>
      <Option type="QString" value="Version Control&#xa;V.1.0.0 - 20.01.25&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.0 - 13.02.35&#xa;- Added attributes &quot;minH&quot; and &quot;maxH&quot; containing a features minimum Height and maxH maximum Height measurement. &#xa;- Added attributes &quot;minHstamp&quot; and &quot;maxHstamp&quot; as datum strings.&#xa;- Added attribute &quot;originfile&quot; containing the name of the input_file. &#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.1 - 13.02.35&#xa;- Separated Chronos and Archimedes&#xa;- added find-nr. and sample-nr. attributefield to pointdata&#xa;- added if-funtion to field_5 for 'null'-values to become '---'&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.2 - 04.04.2025&#xa;- Deleted Doublettes-output: e.g. shptype '03' and '93' will henceforth only be a part of polygons-ouput.&#xa;- 'ID' now is 5-digits long. Future update AS4QGIS12 --> 12 digit sitring&#xa;- added shptype '33', which is a closed polyline and will only be an output of polyline.shp&#xa;- added option to not only measure postholes with '61', but also '06'&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.3 - 12.04.2025&#xa;- Changed shptype funnel of '53' and '73' to be outputed as polygons rather than polylines.&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.4 - 18.06.2025&#xa;- The range of algorithm versions has been reduced from 6 to 3. The distinction between the non-stylized and the stylized [enhanced] version has been removed. Stylization now takes place outside of the algorithm via a right-click on the desired model and the 'Edit Rendering Styles for Outputs...' button in the drop-down menu. Then, in the pop-up window, the corresponding path to the respective style files is specified.&#xa;- Posthole measurements are now also defined as elevation points.&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.5 - 01.07.2025&#xa;- When creating the pseudodata, no threshold values had been considered so far. Now, all decimal values of maxH and minH from X.000 m to X.999 m are assigned to a pseudomonth from January to October.&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.6 - 30.07.2025&#xa;- Previously, in E.7 (Adjust Field Names Polylines) and G.4 (Adjust Field Names Polygons), the fields &quot;maxH&quot; and &quot;minH&quot; were set to the data type decimal (double) with length = 0 and precision = 3. This configuration caused an issue where, upon saving the output layers, the values for &quot;maxH&quot; and &quot;minH&quot; were automatically set to 1,000. This bug has been fixed by updating the field definitions to use a length = 20.&#xa;- Similarly,  in B.2 (Adjust Fields Vertices) and C.9 (Adjust Field Names Pointdata), the decimal (double) fields &quot;x&quot;, &quot;y&quot;, and &quot;z&quot; were also updated to use length = 20 and precision = 3 to ensure correct value storage and prevent rounding errors.&#xa;- All comments in the Model Designer View of AS4QGIS have been updated.&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.7 - 19.10.2025&#xa;- Attribute table modification: The attribute field &quot;CAD-ID&quot; in the output files polygons.shp, polylines.shp, and pointdata.shp has been replaced with two separate fields: &quot;CAD-ID_1&quot; and &quot;CAD-ID_2&quot;. Previously, &quot;CAD-ID&quot; was a concatenation of the attributes &quot;IDstring&quot; and &quot;designatio&quot; (e.g. '0257VF'). Starting with this update, &quot;CAD-ID_1&quot; serves as the direct successor to the original &quot;CAD-ID&quot;, but now includes an underscore _ between &quot;IDstring&quot; and &quot;designatio&quot; (e.g. '0257_VF').&quot;CAD-ID_2&quot;, on the other hand, reverses the order of these attributes (e.g. 'VF_0257'). The purpose of this change is to give users more flexibility — for example, they can use &quot;field_5&quot; = &quot;designatio&quot; as the trench name. For instance, if &quot;field_1&quot; = '0257A03001' and &quot;field_5&quot; = 'F07', then &quot;CAD-ID_2&quot; = 'F07_0257'.&#xa;- Sector A: &quot;IDstring&quot;, &quot;CAD-ID_1&quot;, and &quot;CAD-ID_2&quot; generation was moved to sector A within the algorithm pipeline.&#xa;- Attribute table modification: vertices.shp hence forth also includes the attribute fields &quot;IDstring&quot;, &quot;CAD-ID_1&quot; and &quot;CAD-ID_2&quot;&#xa;- New attribute: The EPSG code of the source data is now stored as an attribute in all generated output files.&#xa;- Totalstation setup coordinates / Change in &quot;shptype_n&quot; of pointdata.shp output: It is now possible to include (total) station setups in pointdata.shp. The algorithm checks &quot;field_1&quot; for the presence of a full stop (.), an underscore (_), or a hyphen (-). If a value in &quot;field_1&quot; contains any of these symbols, the coordinate will be stored with &quot;shptype_n&quot; = 'station_setup'. This allows users to define total station setups using the date followed by the setup number, e.g. '20251019_1', '19990727.14', or '20300417-7'.&#xa;- Sector T: The Pseudo-Date Generator has now been streamlined—based on Claude AI’s suggestion—from 14 algorithms down to just two, which should significantly improve AS4QGIS’s efficiency.&#xa;- Sector A / Code Split 2: &quot;maxH&quot; and &quot;minH&quot;, grouped by &quot;ID&quot;, are now processed using an aggregate function, which should improve the overall efficiency of the algorithm pipeline.&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.8 - 19.12.2025&#xa;Changes have been implemented to improve algorithm simplification, workflow quality,  and terminological consistency:&#xa;- Previously, &quot;shptypes&quot; were assigned to a specific Shptype pipeline via six different extract algorithms. This is now handled by a single feature filter algorithm.&#xa;- A model help text has been added to the algorithm.&#xa;- Output layer names are now generated without the '.shp' suffix.&#xa;- The order of the output layers has been adjusted.&#xa;- Output layers are now generated within the &quot;charted_spatial_records&quot; group.&#xa;- The AS4QGIS default styles now use a controlled feature rendering order, based on “maxH” for polygons and polylines, and on “z” for point data.&#xa;&#xa;V.1.1.9 - 15.01.2026 &quot;Synthesis Update&quot;&#xa;With this version, the previously separate algorithmic workflows have been consolidated into a single unified model named Synthesis.&#xa;- The duplicate version name has been removed. The algorithm group name no longer includes the version number, while the algorithm itself retains versioning.&#xa;- The Model Designer algorithm and documentation layout have been reworked.&#xa;- Several parser algorithms have been consolidated into a single “Refactor Fields” algorithm in order to reduce the overall number of processing steps.&#xa;- The algorithm UI now includes the drop-down menus “ArchSurv-String” and “Code”,  as well as the checkbox “mirror polygon geometries to polylines”.&#xa;- Parameter selection via the drop-down menus renders the previous .csv delimited text import workflow obsolete.  Prior to this update, input data had to follow the strict field order &quot;field_1&quot;, &quot;field_2&quot;, &quot;field_3&quot;, &quot;field_4&quot;, &quot;field_5&quot; (&quot;ArchSurv-String&quot;, &quot;easting/x&quot;, &quot;northing/y&quot;, &quot;elevation/z&quot;, &quot;Code&quot;).&#xa;With the new parameter-based approach,  any point geometry layer can be processed,  provided it contains an attribute column holding the “ArchSurv-String” and,  optionally,  a “Code” column.&#xa;Selection of the “ArchSurv-String” parameter is mandatory,  while the “Code” parameter is optional.&#xa;If no attribute column is assigned to the “Code” parameter, all subsequent calculations are performed using the assumed default value '---'.&#xa;- The checkbox “mirror polygon geometries to polylines” replaces the former Chimaira algorithm. When enabled,  all polygon geometries are duplicated and written to the polyline output layer,  creating a comprehensive master polyline dataset.&#xa;- Three output attribute names were standardized: &quot;designatio&quot; → &quot;code&quot;; &quot;CAD_ID-1&quot; → &quot;ID_code&quot;; &quot;CAD_ID-2&quot; → &quot;code_ID&quot;&#xa;&#xa;V.1.2.0 - 28.02.2026 (Point-ID Conflict Update)&#xa;A dedicated three-step validation pipeline (W.0–W.3) has been added between A.0 and A.1 to detect non-unique Point-IDs in the input dataset prior to geometry generation.&#xa;- W.0 pre-filter added to restrict duplicate checking to polyline and polygon geometries only.&#xa;- W.1 PointID frequency analysis: Counts the number of occurrences of each unique Point-ID in the input dataset by running a statistical category analysis on field_1.&#xa;- W.2 Extract non_unique PointIDs: Filters the frequency table produced by W.1 to retain only those Point-IDs with a count greater than 1, writing the result to the point_id_conflicts output layer.&#xa;- W.3 Raise warning: non-unique Point-IDs: Evaluates whether the point_id_conflicts layer contains any features and, if so, issues a processing log warning instructing the user to resolve the detected Point-ID conflicts in the source file before re-running the algorithm.&#xa;- New Output | point_id_conflicts: A new output layer listing all Point-IDs that appear more than once in the input dataset, together with their occurrence count. If empty, all Point-IDs are unique and no action is required.&#xa;(!) Duplicate Point-ID detection operates on the raw input after A.0 refactoring. The algorithm does not automatically resolve conflicts — manual correction of the source file remains required.&#xa;(!) Workflow tip: To automatically display the feature count of the point_id_conflicts output layer in the Layer Panel, enable Preferences → Canvas &amp; Legend → Layer Legend → Show feature count for newly added layers." name="component_description"/>
      <Option type="double" value="2276.4476030454" name="component_height"/>
      <Option type="double" value="3314.89224821106" name="component_pos_x"/>
      <Option type="double" value="1203.982052417628" name="component_pos_y"/>
